# Observations. The log itself is not carried in git: one census is ~300 MB and
# git never forgets, so a week of them would exceed what GitHub is willing to
# hold. The signed tree heads in heads/ are what gets published -- a few hundred
# bytes a day -- and there git's refusal to forget becomes the point.
data/

# The signing key. If this ever reaches a public repository the log is finished:
# anyone could forge a head, and every head already published becomes worthless
# because nobody can tell which were signed by the operator. The .pub beside it
# is meant to be published; the private half never leaves the server.
heads/key
heads/*.key
*.pem

# Build output
*.exe
dist/

# Editor
.vscode/
